   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to the issuance of distinctive plates bearing the words \"Cure Parkinson's Disease\", and to amend the state finance law, in relation to establishing the \"Cure Parkinson's Disease Trust Fund\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S3521",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3521-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 61,
       "fullName": "Michael H. Ranzenhofer",
       "imgName": "406_michael_h._ranzenhofer.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 406,
       "sessionMemberId": 162,
       "sessionYear": 2013,
       "shortName": "RANZENHOFER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-x, amd §508, V & T L; add §99-u, St Fin L.",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3521\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation\nto the issuance of distinctive plates bearing the words \"Cure\nParkinson's Disease\", and to amend the state finance law, in relation to\nestablishing the \"Cure Parkinson's Disease Trust Fund\"\n\nPURPOSE:  To authorize the issuance of distinctive license plates bear-\ning the words \"Cure Parkinson's Disease,\" the proceeds of which, shall\nbe used for Parkinson's Disease research.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Adds a new section 404-x to the vehicle and traffic law to\nauthorize the creation of distinctive \"Cure Parkinson's Disease\" license\nplates. Requires an additional service charge of twenty-five dollars per\nlicense plate, twenty dollars of which shall be deposited to the credit\nof the cure Parkinson's Disease trust fund, to be used for childhood\ncancer research and education projects approved by the commissioner of\nhealth.\n\nSection 2. Amends section 508 of the vehicle and traffic law, by adding\na new subdivision 6, which directs the commissioner to develop license\napplication and renewal forms, which shall solicit a voluntary one\ndollar donation from persons applying for, or renewing a driver's\nlicense at the time of such application or renewal. These donations\nshall be deposited in the cure Parkinson's Disease trust fund.\n\nSection 3. Adds a new section to the 99-u to the state finance law to\nestablish the Cure Parkinson's Disease trust fund.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  Parkinson's Disease is a chronic, progressive disorder\nof the central nervous system for which there is currently no cure.\nWhile there are a number of medications which help slow the progression,\nmany of these medications lose their effects as the disease progresses\nmaking the need for a cure imperative.\n\nThis legislation furthers the goal of finding a cure for Parkinson's\nDisease by using the revenue generated by the \"Cure Parkinson's Disease\"\nlicense plates, as well as the donations elicited by the commissioner of\nthe Department of Motor Vehicles, to be used for Parkinson's research\nand education projects.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  2011-12 S.2934/A.4518; 2009-10 S.2692/A.6136;\n2007-08, S.2367/A.4462.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth\nday after it shall have become a law provided, however, that the addi-\ntion, amendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary for\n\nthe implementation for this act on its effective date is authorized to\nbe made and completed on or before such date.\n\n",
