    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3521A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to the issuance of distinctive plates bearing the words \"Cure\nParkinson's Disease\", and to amend the state finance law, in relation\nto establishing the \"Cure Parkinson's Disease Trust Fund\"\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the issuance of distinctive license plates bearing the\nwords \"Cure Parkinson's Disease,\" the proceeds of which, shall be used\nfor Parkinson's Disease research.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Adds a new section 404-x to the vehicle and traffic law to\nauthorize the creation of distinctive \"Cure Parkinson's Disease\"\nlicense plates. Requires an additional service charge of twenty-five\ndollars per license plate, twenty dollars of which shall be deposited\nto the credit of the cure Parkinson's Disease trust fund, to be used\nfor childhood cancer research and education projects approved by the\ncommissioner of health.\n\nSection 2. Amends section 508 of the vehicle and traffic law, by\nadding a new subdivision 6, which directs the commissioner to develop\nlicense application and renewal forms, which shall solicit a voluntary\none dollar donation from persons applying for, or renewing a driver's\nlicense at the time of such application or renewal. These donations\nshall be deposited in the cure Parkinson's Disease trust fund.\n\nSection 3. Adds a new section to the 99-w to the state finance law to\nestablish the Cure Parkinson's Disease trust fund.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nParkinson's Disease is a chronic, progressive disorder of the central\nnervous system for which there is currently no cure. While there are a\nnumber of medications which help slow the progression, many of these\nmedications lose their effects as the disease progresses making the\nneed for a cure imperative.\n\nThis legislation furthers the goal of finding a cure for Parkinson's\nDisease by using the revenue generated by the \"Cure Parkinson's\nDisease\" license plates, as well as the donations elicited by the\ncommissioner of the Department of Motor Vehicles, to be used for\nParkinson's research and education projects.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2011-12 S.2934/A.4518;\n2009-10 S.2692/A.6136;\n2007-08, S.2367/A.4462.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall have become a law provided, however, that the addition,\namendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary for the\nimplementation for this act on its effective date is authorized to be\nmade and completed on or before such date.\n\n",
